# .cursor/rules/project.mdc

These constraints apply to every change in this repo. Do not violate them
even if a prompt doesn't repeat them.

- Never add a JS framework, CSS framework, or bundler (React, Vue, Tailwind,
  Bootstrap, webpack, esbuild) without being explicitly asked in the prompt.
- Never add a client-side JS dependency without checking ARCHITECTURE.md
  and SPEC.md first. Pages must work without JavaScript; existing scripts
  are progressive enhancement only.
- CSS follows docs/CSS_ARCHITECTURE.md: BEM class names, SMACSS sheet
  roles, and CSS custom properties in `src/css/tokens.css`. Do not use that
  document's CSS-in-JS, Tailwind / utility-first, or preprocessor examples.
  Visual tokens, motion, and banned looks still come from DESIGN.md.
- Any animation must follow DESIGN.md's motion rules exactly, including the
  prefers-reduced-motion gating.
- Follow the file structure in ARCHITECTURE.md. `_11ty/` is the Eleventy
  helper folder. Don't create other top-level folders or a `components/`
  directory without asking.
- Before making changes across more than one file, propose a short plan and
  wait for approval (use Plan mode).
- After any change, confirm the page still renders correctly and is fully
  navigable with JavaScript disabled.
- Prefer the simplest implementation. If you're about to add a dependency
  to solve something, pause and ask whether plain HTML/CSS/Eleventy can do
  it first.
- Treat the "Explicitly banned patterns" list in DESIGN.md as hard
  constraints, not suggestions. If you're about to add a gradient, a blob
  shape, a glassmorphism card, or a drop-shadow-on-everything look, stop —
  that's the wrong direction for this project even if it looks polished in
  isolation. When in doubt, prefer plainer and flatter over more decorated.
